[b]Good Genes[/b]

Pass parental skills, mutations and higher base stats to kittens, and protect occupied mutation slots during events and combat.

[b]Breeding[/b]
[list]
[*]Kittens inherit two distinct parental active skills when available, or one when only one unique skill is available, plus one eligible parental passive.
[*]Skills are chosen randomly from both parents' combined unique skills. Stimulation does not affect their inheritance chance or favor class skills. Skill-slot limits are unchanged.
[*]Active skills lose their upgrades as in the base game. Skill Share itself is excluded from ordinary passive inheritance; its native upgraded-parent exception remains. With no eligible parental skill, the normal starting skill for that category is retained.
[*]A mutated parent part takes priority over an unmutated parent part.
[*]If both parents have a mutation in the same part, either can be inherited. Special mutations and birth defects are not ranked by strength.
[*]Each base stat inherits the higher of the parents' two values.
[*]Random loss of part inheritance at birth is disabled.
[*]New birth defects and newly generated birth disorders are prevented. Existing parental defects and disorders can still be inherited.
[/list]
Left and right arms, legs, eyes, eyebrows and ears retain separate inherited parts when either side has a mutation. When both inherited sides are ordinary, the pair uses the game's normal mirroring, keeping their appearances matched. This is decided separately for each pair. Unknown part definitions retain their separate inherited appearances. If both parents have different mutations on the same side, the kitten inherits one of them. Matching paired mutations still count once, and the inherited head can hide facial parts and their effects. No extra mutation slots are added.

[b]Event and combat mutations[/b]
Stat-only replacements happen automatically when no stat decreases and at least one increases. Equal changes and pure downgrades keep the current mutation. Trade-offs that increase some stats and decrease others open a Keep Existing / Replace comparison. Matching paired mutations count once when comparing bonuses.

If either the current or incoming mutation has a special effect, an in-game comparison lets you choose Keep Existing or Replace. Keeping the current mutation consumes the roll; it does not reroll.

Both columns show inherited base stats plus active mutation bonuses for the whole change. Incoming increases are green, decreases red, and unchanged values use the normal color. Class bonuses, levels, equipment, and temporary effects are excluded.

Head changes account for facial mutations they hide or restore. Arrows appear only between different affected parts, with full descriptions instead of text paging. Unknown definitions or descriptions too long to show in full keep the existing mutation.

Empty parts behave normally unless a head change also affects an existing facial mutation. Ordinary overnight house mutations are unchanged.

[b]Installation and compatibility[/b]
Requires the native loader listed under Requirements (API 3 or later) and Windows Steam build 1.1.21239 / 25143593.

Install and enable the archive through your mod manager. Enable both its native DLL and asset entry. Close the game before installing, updating, or removing it, and back up your saves.

The mod disables itself on unsupported game builds or when its matching UI assets are not enabled. Native mods that change the same breeding functions may conflict. Removing this mod does not undo changes already saved.

Comparison labels are English. Mutation descriptions use the game's loaded text.

[b]Checking activation[/b]
In mod_logs/chainloader.log, look for [GoodGenes] 0.3.2 enabled. Each birth also logs inherited base stats, selected parental skills and part IDs, with paired IDs listed left/right before head visibility is applied. An unknown parental definition logs a fallback to native inheritance. A DLL-loading line alone does not confirm activation.

Not every scenario has been tested. Bug reports and feedback are welcome in the Bugs and Posts tabs.

